Feature: Checkout Payment Amount Integrity and Order-Payment State Consistency
  As an e-commerce customer
  I want the checkout to charge the correct amount and keep order status consistent with payment status
  So that I am never over/undercharged or left with a confirmed order when payment has not succeeded

  Background:
    Given the customer has a cart containing at least one stock-limited item
    And sandbox test bank credentials are configured for the payment gateway

  @smoke @critical @risk-critical
  Scenario: Gateway request amount reflects combined promo discount and stock-adjusted price
    Given a cart total with an applied promo discount and a stock-adjusted item price
    When the customer submits payment at checkout
    Then the amount sent to the payment gateway equals the cart total minus the promo discount, adjusted for stock-limited pricing
    And the order confirmation displays that same charged amount

  @regression @risk-high
  Scenario: Order remains unconfirmed when stock depletes between authorization and capture
    Given a payment has been authorized for the last remaining unit of an item
    When the stock quantity depletes to zero before capture completes
    Then the payment capture does not proceed and the authorization is reversed
    And the order status stays "not confirmed" with no confirmed order recorded against an uncaptured payment

  @negative @security @risk-medium
  Scenario: CVV is never exposed when a stock-out error occurs mid-payment
    Given the customer has entered card details including CVV at checkout
    When a stock-out error occurs mid-payment
    Then the CVV does not appear in the UI, the error message, or the application log
    And the card number shown is masked to first 6 and last 4 digits only

  @regression @data-driven @risk-critical
  Scenario Outline: Charged amount is computed correctly across promo and stock combinations
    Given a cart with "<promo_status>" and "<stock_status>"
    When the customer completes checkout payment
    Then the amount sent to the gateway equals "<expected_amount_basis>"

    Examples:
      | promo_status              | stock_status                   | expected_amount_basis                          |
      | active promo code applied | sufficient stock               | cart total minus promo discount                |
      | no promo code applied     | stock-limited last-item price  | stock-adjusted item price                      |
      | active promo code applied | stock-limited last-item price  | stock-adjusted price minus promo discount      |

  @boundary @edge-case @risk-medium
  Scenario: Oversized promo code input is safely rejected
    Given the promo code field has a defined maximum accepted length
    When the customer enters a promo code exceeding that maximum length
    Then the checkout rejects the input with a generic validation message
    And no stack trace or internal system detail is exposed

  @negative @security @risk-medium
  Scenario: Injection-pattern input on the card number field is safely rejected
    Given the customer is on the payment details step
    When the customer enters a script or SQL injection pattern into the card number field
    Then the checkout rejects the input with a generic error message
    And no injected script or query executes or appears in the response

  @regression @data-driven @risk-medium
  Scenario Outline: Promo code discount logic resolves correctly for expiry, stacking, and invalid entry
    Given the customer enters a promo code with condition "<promo_condition>"
    When the customer applies the promo code at checkout
    Then the checkout displays "<expected_result>"
    And the charged amount reflects "<expected_result>"

    Examples:
      | promo_condition                 | expected_result                                   |
      | code expired before today       | invalid/expired message, full cart total charged  |
      | two codes entered for stacking  | only the applicable single-use discount applied   |
      | code does not exist             | invalid code message, full cart total charged     |
